<title>USA: MOUNT PLEASANT, S.C., WON BY BANK OF SOUTH CAROLINA. [CORRECTED 17:45 GMT]</title>
<headline>MOUNT PLEASANT, S.C., WON BY BANK OF SOUTH CAROLINA. [CORRECTED 17:45 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects winner of bonds in headline and text from First Union Capital.)</p>
<p>Bank of South Carolina said it won $1.25 million of Mount Pleasant, S.C., general obligation bond, 1997, with a net interest cost of 4.16 percent (corrects from 4.38 percent).</p>
</text>
